# Exercises the destructive bare-metal install lifecycle's IPMI leg for real,
# through unmodified asmb8_boot/asmb8_power/asmb8_info modules run by a real
# ansible-playbook process -- the one thing
# tests/integration/targets/asmb8_baremetal_install_role's own aliases file
# documents as impossible until an IPMI mock existed. See this target's
# tasks/main.yml header comment for exactly how (a same-process
# pyghmi.ipmi.command.Command double, imported instead of real pyghmi via a
# generated fake pyghmi package placed first on PYTHONPATH -- see
# tests/integration/mock_servers/ipmi_server.py's module docstring) and for
# what is deliberately NOT covered here (the iUSB/.asp media leg, and the
# fine-grained per-step ordering/detach-on-failure assertions, both of which
# tests/unit/plugins/modules/test_asmb8_power_lifecycle.py already covers).
#
# context/controller: this target invokes the controller's own Python
# interpreter directly (via ansible_playbook_python) to run
# run_ipmi_mock.py, and points other tasks' PYTHONPATH at what it generates --
# both need the controller's own environment, not a managed node's.
context/controller
skip/windows
